يَا إِمَامَ الرُّسْلِ يَا سَنَدِي / أَنْتَ بَابُ اللهِ مُعْتَمَدِي
Yā imāma r-rusli yā sanadī / anta bābu llāhi muʿtamadī
O leader of all the Messengers, O my Support — you are the door to Allah, the one on whom I rely.

فَبِدُنْيَايَ وَآخِرَتِي / يَا رَسُولَ اللهِ خُذْ بِيَدِي
Fa-bi-dunyāya wa-ākhiratī / yā rasūla llāhi khudh bi-yadī
So in this my dunya and in my afterlife — O Messenger of Allah, take me by the hand.

قَسَمًا بِالنَّجْمِ حِينَ هَوَى / مَا الْمُعَافَى وَالسَّقِيمُ سَوَى
Qasaman bi-n-najmi ḥīna hawā / mā l-muʿāfā wa-s-saqīmu sawā
An oath, by the star when it declines — the sound in health and the sick are not alike.

فَاخْلَعِ الْكَوْنَيْنِ عَنْكَ سِوَى / حُبِّ مَوْلَى الْعُرْبِ وَالْعَجَمِ
Fa-khlaʿi l-kawnayni ʿanka siwā / ḥubbi mawlā l-ʿurbi wa-l-ʿajami
So strip the two worlds from yourself, save only love of the Master of the Arabs and the non-Arabs.

سَيِّدُ السَّادَاتِ مِنْ مُضَرٍ / غَوْثُ أَهْلِ الْبَدْوِ وَالْحَضَرِ
Sayyidu s-sādāti min muḍarin / ghawthu ahli l-badwi wa-l-ḥaḍari
Master of masters, from Muḍar — the succour of the people of the desert and of the settled towns.

صَاحِبُ الْآيَاتِ وَالسُّوَرِ / مَنْبَعُ الْأَحْكَامِ وَالْحِكَمِ
Ṣāḥibu l-āyāti wa-s-suwari / manbaʿu l-aḥkāmi wa-l-ḥikami
Possessor of the verses and the sūras — the wellspring of the rulings and of wisdom.

قَمَرٌ طَابَتْ سَرِيرَتُهُ / وَسَجَايَاهُ وَسِيرَتُهُ
Qamarun ṭābat sarīratuhu / wa sajāyāhu wa sīratuhu
A moon whose inmost heart was pure — and his inborn qualities, and his way of life.

صَفْوَةُ الْبَارِي وَخِيرَتُهُ / عَدْلُ أَهْلِ الْحِلِّ وَالْحَرَمِ
Ṣafwatu l-bārī wa khīratuhu / ʿadlu ahli l-ḥilli wa-l-ḥarami
The chosen and elect of the Creator — the upright witness for the people of the profane lands and of the Sanctuary.

مَا رَأَتْ عَيْنٌ وَلَيْسَ تَرَى / مِثْلَ طَهَ فِي الْوَرَى بَشَرَا
Mā raʾat ʿaynun wa laysa tarā / mithla Ṭāhā fi l-warā basharā
No eye has seen, nor will it ever see, a human being like Ṭāhā among creation.

خَيْرُ مَنْ فَوْقَ الثَّرَى أَثَرَا / طَاهِرُ الْأَخْلَاقِ وَالشِّيَمِ
Khayru man fawqa th-tharā atharā / ṭāhiru l-akhlāqi wa-sh-shiyami
Best of all who left a trace upon the earth — pure in character and in noble traits.
